<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday, it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc,</p>
<p>$500 million mortgaged due 2007,</p>
<p>one billion marks mortgaged due 2002.</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Ibiden Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002.  </p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Senko Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2004.</p>
<p>Taisei Oncho Co Ltd, 0.42 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.</p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Catena Corp, 0.35 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.</p>
<p>Himaraya Co Ltd, 40 million Swiss Francs unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement.  </p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Muraki Corp, 0.11 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.</p>
<p>NKK Corp, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2007.</p>
</text>
